      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the given problem, we start with the system of equations:\n\n\\[\nx + y = 4\n\\]\n\\[\n3xy = 4 \\implies xy = \\frac{4}{3}\n\\]\n\nWe can treat \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) as the roots of the quadratic equation \\(t^2 - (x+y)t + xy = 0\\). Substituting the known values, we get:\n\n\\[\nt^2 - 4t + \\frac{4}{3} = 0\n\\]\n\nTo clear the fraction, we multiply through by 3:\n\n\\[\n3t^2 - 12t + 4 = 0\n\\]\n\nWe solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\(t = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\), where \\(a = 3\\), \\(b = -12\\), and \\(c = 4\\):\n\n\\[\nt = \\frac{12 \\pm \\sqrt{144 - 48}}{6} = \\frac{12 \\pm \\sqrt{96}}{6} = \\frac{12 \\pm 4\\sqrt{6}}{6} = \\frac{6 \\pm 2\\sqrt{6}}{3} = 2 \\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, the solutions for \\(x\\) are:\n\n\\[\nx = 2 + \\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad x = 2 - \\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3}\n\\]\n\nRewriting these solutions in the form \\(x = \\frac{a \\pm b\\sqrt{c}}{d}\\), we identify \\(a = 6\\), \\(b = 2\\), \\(c = 6\\), and \\(d = 3\\). Therefore, \\(a + b + c + d = 6 + 2 + 6 + 3 = 17\\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{17}\n\\]",
